# ============================================================
#  BME Project — .gitignore
#  RULE: no patient data, no imaging files, no model weights in git.
#  Imaging lives in object storage / DVC. Git holds code + docs only.
# ============================================================

# ---------- PATIENT DATA (PHI) — NEVER COMMIT ----------
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. Without it, `BME/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth — and git is case-insensitive on Windows —
# which silently swallowed the `ml/src/bme/` Python package. Keep the slashes.
# Safety does not depend on these alone: the imaging extensions below are
# unanchored and catch a stray scan wherever it lands.
/BME/
/Non BME/
/data/
/datasets/
/raw/
/interim/
/processed/
/phi/
*_PHI*

# Reference papers — the PDFs are copyrighted and not ours to redistribute,
# but our own analysis of them is our work and belongs in the repo.
/RP/*
!/RP/ANALYSIS.md
/papers/
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf
deid_map.csv
deid_map.json

# Medical imaging formats (belt-and-braces, in case data moves)
*.dcm
*.DCM
*.dicom
*.ima
*.IMA
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.nrrd
*.nhdr
*.seg.nrrd
*.mha
*.mhd
*.img
*.hdr
*.mrb
*.mrml
*.gipl
DICOMDIR

